### convert_i32

<!-- livebook:{"chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.Spiral.Cells.SmartCell","attrs":{"timeout":300,"source":":= is_string_type \\* t. (_ : t) : bool = ~> ?: t ?| string => !+ | _ => !-\n:= is_float_type \\* t. (_ : t) : bool = ~> ?: t ?| f64 => !+ | f32 => !+ | _ => !-\n\n:= convert_i32 \\* t. (x : t) : int =\n    backend_switch {\n        Gleam = \\ () => x |> convert_i32_base 10 : int\n        Lua = \\ () => x |> convert_i32_base 10 : int\n        Fsharp = \\ () => $'System.Convert.ToInt32(!x)' : int\n        Python = \\ () => x |> convert_i32_base 10 : int\n        Rust = \\ () =>\n            ? (~> ?: t ?| string => !+ | _ => !-)\n            ?> x |> convert_i32_base 10 : int\n            |? (~> ?: t ?| f64 => !+ | f32 => !+ | _ => !-)\n            ?> $'((!x).round_ties_even() as i32)' : int\n            |: $'(!x as i32)' : int\n        C = \\ () =>\n            ? is_string_type x\n            ?> x |> convert_i32_base 10 : int\n            |? is_float_type x ?>\n                global \"#include <math.h>\"\n                $'(int32_t)nearbyint(!x)' : int\n            |: $'(int32_t)(!x)' : int\n        Pascal = \\ () =>\n            ? is_string_type x\n            ?> x |> convert_i32_base 10 : int\n            |? is_float_type x\n            ?> $'Round(!x)' : int\n            |: $'Int32(!x)' : int\n        TypeScript = \\ () =>\n            ? is_string_type x\n            ?> x |> convert_i32_base 10 : int\n            |? is_float_type x\n            ?> $'backend_switch_has_no_TypeScript_float_rounding_in_lib_spiral' : int\n            |: $'Number(!x)' : int\n        Wasm = \\ () =>\n            ? is_string_type x\n            ?> x |> convert_i32_base 10 : int\n            |? is_float_type x\n            ?> $'(i32.trunc_sat_f64_s (f64.nearest !x))' : int\n            |: x |> numeric_conv : int\n        Zig = \\ () =>\n            ? is_string_type x\n            ?> x |> convert_i32_base 10 : int\n            |? is_float_type x\n            then $'\\@as(i32, \\@intFromFloat(if (\\@abs(!x - \\@trunc(!x)) == 0.5) 2.0 * \\@round(!x / 2.0) else \\\n                \\@round(!x)))' : int\n            |: x |> numeric_conv : int\n        Lean = \\ () =>\n            ? is_string_type x\n            ?> x |> convert_i32_base 10 : int\n            |? is_float_type x\n            ?> $'backend_switch_has_no_Lean_float_rounding_in_lib_spiral' : int\n            |: $'(Int32.ofInt (SpiralToInt.toI !x))' : int\n        Kotlin = \\ () =>\n            ? is_string_type x\n            ?> x |> convert_i32_base 10 : int\n            |? is_float_type x\n            ?> $'kotlin.math.round(!x).toInt()' : int\n            |: $'(!x).toInt()' : int\n        Swift = \\ () =>\n            ? is_string_type x\n            ?> x |> convert_i32_base 10 : int\n            |? is_float_type x\n            ?> $'Int32((!x).rounded(.toNearestOrEven))' : int\n            |: $'Int32(truncatingIfNeeded: !x)' : int\n    }","print_code":false},"livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Spiral.Cells.eval!(
  ~S"""
  := is_string_type \* t. (_ : t) : bool = ~> ?: t ?| string => !+ | _ => !-
  := is_float_type \* t. (_ : t) : bool = ~> ?: t ?| f64 => !+ | f32 => !+ | _ => !-

  := convert_i32 \* t. (x : t) : int =
      backend_switch {
          Gleam = \ () => x |> convert_i32_base 10 : int
          Lua = \ () => x |> convert_i32_base 10 : int
          Fsharp = \ () => $'System.Convert.ToInt32(!x)' : int
          Python = \ () => x |> convert_i32_base 10 : int
          Rust = \ () =>
              ? (~> ?: t ?| string => !+ | _ => !-)
              ?> x |> convert_i32_base 10 : int
              |? (~> ?: t ?| f64 => !+ | f32 => !+ | _ => !-)
              ?> $'((!x).round_ties_even() as i32)' : int
              |: $'(!x as i32)' : int
          C = \ () =>
              ? is_string_type x
              ?> x |> convert_i32_base 10 : int
              |? is_float_type x ?>
                  global "#include <math.h>"
                  $'(int32_t)nearbyint(!x)' : int
              |: $'(int32_t)(!x)' : int
          Pascal = \ () =>
              ? is_string_type x
              ?> x |> convert_i32_base 10 : int
              |? is_float_type x
              ?> $'Round(!x)' : int
              |: $'Int32(!x)' : int
          TypeScript = \ () =>
              ? is_string_type x
              ?> x |> convert_i32_base 10 : int
              |? is_float_type x
              ?> $'backend_switch_has_no_TypeScript_float_rounding_in_lib_spiral' : int
              |: $'Number(!x)' : int
          Wasm = \ () =>
              ? is_string_type x
              ?> x |> convert_i32_base 10 : int
              |? is_float_type x
              ?> $'(i32.trunc_sat_f64_s (f64.nearest !x))' : int
              |: x |> numeric_conv : int
          Zig = \ () =>
              ? is_string_type x
              ?> x |> convert_i32_base 10 : int
              |? is_float_type x
              then $'\@as(i32, \@intFromFloat(if (\@abs(!x - \@trunc(!x)) == 0.5) 2.0 * \@round(!x / 2.0) else \
                  \@round(!x)))' : int
              |: x |> numeric_conv : int
          Lean = \ () =>
              ? is_string_type x
              ?> x |> convert_i32_base 10 : int
              |? is_float_type x
              ?> $'backend_switch_has_no_Lean_float_rounding_in_lib_spiral' : int
              |: $'(Int32.ofInt (SpiralToInt.toI !x))' : int
          Kotlin = \ () =>
              ? is_string_type x
              ?> x |> convert_i32_base 10 : int
              |? is_float_type x
              ?> $'kotlin.math.round(!x).toInt()' : int
              |: $'(!x).toInt()' : int
          Swift = \ () =>
              ? is_string_type x
              ?> x |> convert_i32_base 10 : int
              |? is_float_type x
              ?> $'Int32((!x).rounded(.toNearestOrEven))' : int
              |: $'Int32(truncatingIfNeeded: !x)' : int
      }
  """,
  timeout: 300_000
)
```

### try_convert

<!-- livebook:{"chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.Spiral.Cells.SmartCell","attrs":{"timeout":300,"source":":= integer_fits \\* u. (_ : u) (value : i64) : bool =\n    := bounded : bool = ~> ?: u ?| i64 => !- | u64 => !- | _ => !+\n    := lowest : i64 = ~> ?: u ?| i8 => -128i64 | i16 => -32768i64 | i32 => -2147483648i64 | _ => 0i64\n    := highest : i64 =\n        ~>\n            ?: u ?|\n            | i8 => 127i64\n            | i16 => 32767i64\n            | i32 => 2147483647i64\n            | u8 => 255i64\n            | u16 => 65535i64\n            | u32 => 4294967295i64\n            | _ => 0i64\n    not bounded || (value >= lowest && value <= highest)\n\n:= parsed_integer \\* u. (ok : bool) (value : i64) : option u =\n    := integral : bool =\n        ~>\n            ?: u ?|\n            | i8 => !+\n            | i16 => !+\n            | i32 => !+\n            | i64 => !+\n            | u8 => !+\n            | u16 => !+\n            | u32 => !+\n            | u64 => !+\n            | _ => !-\n    ? integral ?>\n        := converted : u = ~> conv `i64 `u value\n        ? ok && integer_fits converted value ?> Some converted |: None\n    |: None\n\n:= narrow_parsed \\* u. (ok : bool) (value : f64) : option u =\n    := low, high =\n        ~>\n            ?: u ?|\n            | i8 => -128.0f64, 127.0f64\n            | i16 => -32768.0f64, 32767.0f64\n            | i32 => -2147483648.0f64, 2147483647.0f64\n            | u8 => 0.0f64, 255.0f64\n            | u16 => 0.0f64, 65535.0f64\n            | _ => 0.0f64, 4294967295.0f64\n    := converted : u = ~> conv `f64 `u value\n    ? ok && value >= low && value <= high ?> Some converted |: None\n\n:= try_convert \\* t u. (x : t) : option u =\n    x\n    |> to' \\ x =>\n        backend_switch {\n            Gleam = \\ () =>\n                ?\n                    is_string_type x\n                    && (\n                        ~>\n                            ?: u ?|\n                            | i8 => !+\n                            | i16 => !+\n                            | i32 => !+\n                            | i64 => !+\n                            | u8 => !+\n                            | u16 => !+\n                            | u32 => !+\n                            | u64 => !+\n                            | _ => !-\n                    )\n                ?>\n                    global \"import gleam/int\"\n                    global \"import gleam/string\"\n                    := (n : int), (err : int) =\n                        $'case int.parse(string.trim(!x)) { Ok(n) -> ##(n, 0) Error(Nil) -> ##(0, 1) }'\n                    ? err = 0\n                    ?> n |> to |> Some\n                    |: None : _ u\n                |: x |> to |> Some\n            Lua = \\ () =>\n                ? is_string_type x ?>\n                    := ok = ($'(string.match(!x, \"^%s*[+-]?%d+%s*$\") ~= nil)' : bool)\n                    := narrow : bool =\n                        ~>\n                            ?: u ?|\n                            | i8 => !+\n                            | i16 => !+\n                            | i32 => !+\n                            | u8 => !+\n                            | u16 => !+\n                            | u32 => !+\n                            | _ => !-\n                    ? narrow\n                    ?> narrow_parsed ok ($'(tonumber(!x) or 0)' : f64)\n                    |: parsed_integer ok ($'(tonumber(!x) or 0)' : i64)\n                |: x |> to |> Some : _ u\n            Fsharp = \\ () =>\n                resultm::from_try\n                    \\ () => $'!x |> `u '\n                    eval\n                |> resultm::ok\n                : _ u\n            Python = \\ () =>\n                resultm::from_try\n                    \\ () => $'`u(!x)'\n                    eval\n                |> resultm::ok\n                : _ u\n            Rust = \\ () =>\n                ? (~> ?: u ?| string => !+ | _ => !-)\n                ?> Some $'Rc::<str>::from(format\\!(\"{}\", !x))'\n                |? (~> ?: t ?| string => !+ | _ => !-) ?>\n                    ($'(!x).trim().parse::<`u>().ok()' : optionm'::option' u) |> optionm'::unbox\n                |: Some $'((!x) as `u)'\n            C = \\ () =>\n                ? is_string_type x ?>\n                    global \"#include <stdbool.h>\"\n                    global \"#include <stdlib.h>\"\n                    global \"#include <ctype.h>\"\n                    global \"#include <errno.h>\"\n                    global (\n                        \"static bool spiral_integer_text_ok(const char *s) { char *end; while (isspace((unsigned \"\n                        ^^ \"char)*s)) s++; if (!*s) return false; errno = 0; strtoll(s, &end, 10); if (errno != 0 || \"\n                        ^^ \"end == s) return false; while (isspace((unsigned char)*end)) end++; return *end == 0; }\"\n                    )\n                    parsed_integer ($'spiral_integer_text_ok((!x)->ptr)' : bool) ($'strtoll((!x)->ptr, NULL, 10)' : i64)\n                |: x |> to |> Some : _ u\n            Pascal = \\ () =>\n                ? is_string_type x ?>\n                    parsed_integer\n                        ($'(StrToInt64Def(Trim(!x), 0) = StrToInt64Def(Trim(!x), 1))' : bool)\n                        ($'StrToInt64Def(Trim(!x), 0)' : i64)\n                |: x |> to |> Some : _ u\n            TypeScript = \\ () =>\n                ? is_string_type x ?>\n                    := ok : bool = $'/^\\\\s*[+-]?\\\\d+\\\\s*$/.test(!x)'\n                    parsed_integer ok ($'(!ok ? BigInt(!x) : 0n)' : i64)\n                |: x |> to |> Some : _ u\n            Wasm = \\ () =>\n                ? is_string_type x ?>\n                    parsed_integer ($'(call $integer_text_ok !x)' : bool) ($'(call $parse_i64 !x (i32.const 10))' : i64)\n                |: x |> to |> Some : _ u\n            Zig = \\ () =>\n                ? is_string_type x ?>\n                    inl ok : bool = $'(if (std.fmt.parseInt(i64, std.mem.trim(u8, !x, \" \\\\t\\\\r\\\\n\"), 10)) |_| true \\\n                        else |_| false)'\n                    parsed_integer ok ($'(std.fmt.parseInt(i64, std.mem.trim(u8, !x, \" \\\\t\\\\r\\\\n\"), 10) catch 0)' : i64)\n                |? (~> ?: t ?| unativeint => !+ | _ => !-) || (~> ?: u ?| unativeint => !+ | _ => !-) ?>\n                    Some ($'@@intCast(!x)' : u)\n                |: x |> numeric_conv |> Some : _ u\n            Lean = \\ () =>\n                ? is_string_type x ?>\n                    lean_parse_helpers ()\n                    parsed_integer ($'(spiralParseInt? !x).isSome' : bool) ($'(Int64.ofInt ((spiralParseInt? !x).getD \\\n                        0))' : i64)\n                |: x |> to |> Some : _ u\n            Kotlin = \\ () =>\n                ? is_string_type x ?>\n                    parsed_integer\n                        ($'((!x).trim().toLongOrNull() \\!= null)' : bool)\n                        ($'((!x).trim().toLongOrNull() ?: 0L)' : i64)\n                |: x |> to |> Some : _ u\n            Swift = \\ () =>\n                ? is_string_type x\n                then parsed_integer ($'((!x).split(separator: \" \").count == 1 && Int64(String((!x).split(separator: \" \\\n                    \")[0])) \\!= nil)' : bool) ($'(Int64(String((!x).split(separator: \" \").first ?? \"\")) ?? 0)' : i64)\n                |: x |> to |> Some : _ u\n        }","print_code":false},"livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Spiral.Cells.eval!(
  ~S"""
  := integer_fits \* u. (_ : u) (value : i64) : bool =
      := bounded : bool = ~> ?: u ?| i64 => !- | u64 => !- | _ => !+
      := lowest : i64 = ~> ?: u ?| i8 => -128i64 | i16 => -32768i64 | i32 => -2147483648i64 | _ => 0i64
      := highest : i64 =
          ~>
              ?: u ?|
              | i8 => 127i64
              | i16 => 32767i64
              | i32 => 2147483647i64
              | u8 => 255i64
              | u16 => 65535i64
              | u32 => 4294967295i64
              | _ => 0i64
      not bounded || (value >= lowest && value <= highest)

  := parsed_integer \* u. (ok : bool) (value : i64) : option u =
      := integral : bool =
          ~>
              ?: u ?|
              | i8 => !+
              | i16 => !+
              | i32 => !+
              | i64 => !+
              | u8 => !+
              | u16 => !+
              | u32 => !+
              | u64 => !+
              | _ => !-
      ? integral ?>
          := converted : u = ~> conv `i64 `u value
          ? ok && integer_fits converted value ?> Some converted |: None
      |: None

  := narrow_parsed \* u. (ok : bool) (value : f64) : option u =
      := low, high =
          ~>
              ?: u ?|
              | i8 => -128.0f64, 127.0f64
              | i16 => -32768.0f64, 32767.0f64
              | i32 => -2147483648.0f64, 2147483647.0f64
              | u8 => 0.0f64, 255.0f64
              | u16 => 0.0f64, 65535.0f64
              | _ => 0.0f64, 4294967295.0f64
      := converted : u = ~> conv `f64 `u value
      ? ok && value >= low && value <= high ?> Some converted |: None

  := try_convert \* t u. (x : t) : option u =
      x
      |> to' \ x =>
          backend_switch {
              Gleam = \ () =>
                  ?
                      is_string_type x
                      && (
                          ~>
                              ?: u ?|
                              | i8 => !+
                              | i16 => !+
                              | i32 => !+
                              | i64 => !+
                              | u8 => !+
                              | u16 => !+
                              | u32 => !+
                              | u64 => !+
                              | _ => !-
                      )
                  ?>
                      global "import gleam/int"
                      global "import gleam/string"
                      := (n : int), (err : int) =
                          $'case int.parse(string.trim(!x)) { Ok(n) -> ##(n, 0) Error(Nil) -> ##(0, 1) }'
                      ? err = 0
                      ?> n |> to |> Some
                      |: None : _ u
                  |: x |> to |> Some
              Lua = \ () =>
                  ? is_string_type x ?>
                      := ok = ($'(string.match(!x, "^%s*[+-]?%d+%s*$") ~= nil)' : bool)
                      := narrow : bool =
                          ~>
                              ?: u ?|
                              | i8 => !+
                              | i16 => !+
                              | i32 => !+
                              | u8 => !+
                              | u16 => !+
                              | u32 => !+
                              | _ => !-
                      ? narrow
                      ?> narrow_parsed ok ($'(tonumber(!x) or 0)' : f64)
                      |: parsed_integer ok ($'(tonumber(!x) or 0)' : i64)
                  |: x |> to |> Some : _ u
              Fsharp = \ () =>
                  resultm::from_try
                      \ () => $'!x |> `u '
                      eval
                  |> resultm::ok
                  : _ u
              Python = \ () =>
                  resultm::from_try
                      \ () => $'`u(!x)'
                      eval
                  |> resultm::ok
                  : _ u
              Rust = \ () =>
                  ? (~> ?: u ?| string => !+ | _ => !-)
                  ?> Some $'Rc::<str>::from(format\!("{}", !x))'
                  |? (~> ?: t ?| string => !+ | _ => !-) ?>
                      ($'(!x).trim().parse::<`u>().ok()' : optionm'::option' u) |> optionm'::unbox
                  |: Some $'((!x) as `u)'
              C = \ () =>
                  ? is_string_type x ?>
                      global "#include <stdbool.h>"
                      global "#include <stdlib.h>"
                      global "#include <ctype.h>"
                      global "#include <errno.h>"
                      global (
                          "static bool spiral_integer_text_ok(const char *s) { char *end; while (isspace((unsigned "
                          ^^ "char)*s)) s++; if (!*s) return false; errno = 0; strtoll(s, &end, 10); if (errno != 0 || "
                          ^^ "end == s) return false; while (isspace((unsigned char)*end)) end++; return *end == 0; }"
                      )
                      parsed_integer ($'spiral_integer_text_ok((!x)->ptr)' : bool) ($'strtoll((!x)->ptr, NULL, 10)' : i64)
                  |: x |> to |> Some : _ u
              Pascal = \ () =>
                  ? is_string_type x ?>
                      parsed_integer
                          ($'(StrToInt64Def(Trim(!x), 0) = StrToInt64Def(Trim(!x), 1))' : bool)
                          ($'StrToInt64Def(Trim(!x), 0)' : i64)
                  |: x |> to |> Some : _ u
              TypeScript = \ () =>
                  ? is_string_type x ?>
                      := ok : bool = $'/^\\s*[+-]?\\d+\\s*$/.test(!x)'
                      parsed_integer ok ($'(!ok ? BigInt(!x) : 0n)' : i64)
                  |: x |> to |> Some : _ u
              Wasm = \ () =>
                  ? is_string_type x ?>
                      parsed_integer ($'(call $integer_text_ok !x)' : bool) ($'(call $parse_i64 !x (i32.const 10))' : i64)
                  |: x |> to |> Some : _ u
              Zig = \ () =>
                  ? is_string_type x ?>
                      inl ok : bool = $'(if (std.fmt.parseInt(i64, std.mem.trim(u8, !x, " \\t\\r\\n"), 10)) |_| true \
                          else |_| false)'
                      parsed_integer ok ($'(std.fmt.parseInt(i64, std.mem.trim(u8, !x, " \\t\\r\\n"), 10) catch 0)' : i64)
                  |? (~> ?: t ?| unativeint => !+ | _ => !-) || (~> ?: u ?| unativeint => !+ | _ => !-) ?>
                      Some ($'@@intCast(!x)' : u)
                  |: x |> numeric_conv |> Some : _ u
              Lean = \ () =>
                  ? is_string_type x ?>
                      lean_parse_helpers ()
                      parsed_integer ($'(spiralParseInt? !x).isSome' : bool) ($'(Int64.ofInt ((spiralParseInt? !x).getD \
                          0))' : i64)
                  |: x |> to |> Some : _ u
              Kotlin = \ () =>
                  ? is_string_type x ?>
                      parsed_integer
                          ($'((!x).trim().toLongOrNull() \!= null)' : bool)
                          ($'((!x).trim().toLongOrNull() ?: 0L)' : i64)
                  |: x |> to |> Some : _ u
              Swift = \ () =>
                  ? is_string_type x
                  then parsed_integer ($'((!x).split(separator: " ").count == 1 && Int64(String((!x).split(separator: " \
                      ")[0])) \!= nil)' : bool) ($'(Int64(String((!x).split(separator: " ").first ?? "")) ?? 0)' : i64)
                  |: x |> to |> Some : _ u
          }
  """,
  timeout: 300_000
)
```

<!-- livebook:{"chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.Spiral.Cells.SmartCell","attrs":{"timeout":300,"source":"///- --test --symbol\n///> gleam\n///> lua\n///> fsharp\n///> rust\n\n3i32\n|> try_convert\n|> optionm::value\n|> _assert_eq' (\n    backend_switch {\n        Gleam = \\ () => ($'3' : unativeint) : unativeint\n        Lua = \\ () => ($'3' : unativeint) : unativeint\n        Fsharp = \\ () => ($'3 |> `unativeint ' : unativeint) : unativeint\n        Python = \\ () => ($'3' : unativeint) : unativeint\n        Rust = \\ () => ($'3usize' : unativeint) : unativeint\n    } : unativeint\n)","print_code":false},"livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Spiral.Cells.eval!(
  ~S"""
  ///- --test --symbol
  ///> gleam
  ///> lua
  ///> fsharp
  ///> rust

  3i32
  |> try_convert
  |> optionm::value
  |> _assert_eq' (
      backend_switch {
          Gleam = \ () => ($'3' : unativeint) : unativeint
          Lua = \ () => ($'3' : unativeint) : unativeint
          Fsharp = \ () => ($'3 |> `unativeint ' : unativeint) : unativeint
          Python = \ () => ($'3' : unativeint) : unativeint
          Rust = \ () => ($'3usize' : unativeint) : unativeint
      } : unativeint
  )
  """,
  timeout: 300_000
)
```

<!-- livebook:{"chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.Spiral.Cells.SmartCell","attrs":{"timeout":300,"source":"///- --test --symbol\n///> gleam\n///> fsharp\n///> rust\n///> cuda\n\n\"3\"\n|> try_convert\n|> _assert_eq (3i32 |> Some)\n\n\"999999999999999\"\n|> try_convert\n|> _assert_eq (999999999999999i64 |> Some)\n\n\"a\"\n|> try_convert\n|> _assert_eq (None : _ int)\n\n!+\n|> try_convert\n|> _assert_eq (1i32 |> Some)\n\n!-\n|> try_convert\n|> _assert_eq (0i32 |> Some)","print_code":false},"livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Spiral.Cells.eval!(
  ~S"""
  ///- --test --symbol
  ///> gleam
  ///> fsharp
  ///> rust
  ///> cuda

  "3"
  |> try_convert
  |> _assert_eq (3i32 |> Some)

  "999999999999999"
  |> try_convert
  |> _assert_eq (999999999999999i64 |> Some)

  "a"
  |> try_convert
  |> _assert_eq (None : _ int)

  !+
  |> try_convert
  |> _assert_eq (1i32 |> Some)

  !-
  |> try_convert
  |> _assert_eq (0i32 |> Some)
  """,
  timeout: 300_000
)
```

#### try_convert_reads_narrow_integers_natively (test)

<!-- livebook:{"chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.Spiral.Cells.SmartCell","attrs":{"timeout":300,"source":"///- --test --symbol\n///> lua\n\n:= ~small = \"3\"\n:= ~negative = \" -12 \"\n:= ~wide = \"2147483648\"\n:= ~fraction = \"1.5\"\n:= ~byte = \"300\"\n:= a, b, c = (try_convert small : option i32), (try_convert negative : option i32), (try_convert wide : option i32)\n:= d, e = (try_convert fraction : option i32), (try_convert byte : option u8)\n(a, b, c, d, e) |> _assert_eq (Some 3i32, Some (0i32 - 12i32), None, None, None)","print_code":false},"livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Spiral.Cells.eval!(
  ~S"""
  ///- --test --symbol
  ///> lua

  := ~small = "3"
  := ~negative = " -12 "
  := ~wide = "2147483648"
  := ~fraction = "1.5"
  := ~byte = "300"
  := a, b, c = (try_convert small : option i32), (try_convert negative : option i32), (try_convert wide : option i32)
  := d, e = (try_convert fraction : option i32), (try_convert byte : option u8)
  (a, b, c, d, e) |> _assert_eq (Some 3i32, Some (0i32 - 12i32), None, None, None)
  """,
  timeout: 300_000
)
```

#### unativeint_round_trip_casts_on_native_backends (test)

<!-- livebook:{"chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.Spiral.Cells.SmartCell","attrs":{"timeout":300,"source":"///- --test --symbol\n///> zig\n///> rust\n\n:= n : unativeint = 3i32 |> try_convert |> optionm::value\n:= back : i32 = n |> try_convert |> optionm::value\nback |> _assert_eq 3i32","print_code":false},"livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Spiral.Cells.eval!(
  ~S"""
  ///- --test --symbol
  ///> zig
  ///> rust

  := n : unativeint = 3i32 |> try_convert |> optionm::value
  := back : i32 = n |> try_convert |> optionm::value
  back |> _assert_eq 3i32
  """,
  timeout: 300_000
)
```

